<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-ph" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-tools/">Free tools</a></li><li aria-current="page">Claim Timeline Planner</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free planner</p><h1>Claim Timeline Planner: An Insurance Claim Deadline Calculator</h1><p class="lede">Policies run on deadlines, and they don’t pause while you negotiate. This insurance claim deadline calculator builds a timeline from your date of loss and exports it to any calendar app.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool" data-tool="dates">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim timeline planner</span><i>Exports an .ics calendar file</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div><label for="t-d">Date of loss</label><input id="t-d" type="date" name="dol"></div>
      <p class="hint flush">Set each window to match your policy and the carrier’s letters. Defaults are common planning figures, not legal advice.</p>
      <div class="days-grid">
        <div><label for="t-n">Report the claim within (days)</label><input id="t-n" name="notice" inputmode="numeric" value="2"></div>
        <div><label for="t-m">Temporary repairs within (days)</label><input id="t-m" name="mitig" inputmode="numeric" value="10"></div>
        <div><label for="t-p">Proof of loss (days)</label><input id="t-p" name="pol" inputmode="numeric" value="60"><span class="hint">Often counted from the insurer’s request.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-r">Replacement-cost repair window (days)</label><input id="t-r" name="rcd" inputmode="numeric" value="180"><span class="hint">Policies vary widely. Check yours.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-s">Suit limitation (days)</label><input id="t-s" name="suit" inputmode="numeric" value="730"><span class="hint">Two years = 730 days.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <ol class="timeline" data-o="timeline"></ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn small" data-ics>Download .ics calendar file</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The dates that quietly decide claims</h2>
<p>Most claim problems we see aren’t about the estimate at all — they’re about a window that closed. Notice, proof of loss, the time to complete repairs for replacement cost, and the policy’s suit-limitation period all run from different starting points. Missing one can cost far more than any line item.</p>
<h2>How to use this insurance claim deadline calculator</h2>
<ol>
<li>Enter the date of loss (the hail or wind date, the day the pipe burst, or the day you found the ice-dam leak).</li>
<li>Adjust each window to match your policy and any letters from the insurer.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Download .ics</strong> to add the milestones to Google, Apple or Outlook calendars.</li>
</ol>
<h2>About Minnesota suit limitations</h2>
<p>Minnesota’s standard fire policy language commonly limits lawsuits to two years after the loss, and many policies repeat that. Some policies or circumstances differ. Read the “Suit Against Us” condition and talk with a Minnesota attorney well before the date — appraisal doesn’t automatically extend it.</p>
<p>The planner is a reminder tool only. It does not calculate legal deadlines for you.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the date of loss the day I noticed the damage?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually it is the day the damage happened, such as the storm date. For gradual or hidden damage, the policy and the facts decide, so note both dates.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does invoking appraisal pause the suit deadline?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Don’t assume it does. Ask a Minnesota attorney how the deadline applies to your situation before it gets close.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my data saved?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The planner runs in your browser and the calendar file is generated on your device.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/free-tools/appraisal-readiness-checkup/"><small>Checklist</small><span>Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/free-tools/roof-snow-load-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Snow Load Calculator</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentC